The graph shows the declining-balance value of a metal lathe.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}\begin{axis}[width=7.6cm,height=5.8cm,axis lines=left,axis line style={-{Stealth}},xmin=0,xmax=4.6,ymin=0,ymax=33000,xtick={0,1,2,3,4},ytick={0,7500,15000,22500,30000},grid=both,clip=false,scaled ticks=false,ticklabel style={font=\scriptsize,/pgf/number format/fixed},xlabel={Years, $n$},ylabel={Value (\$)},title={Metal lathe value}]
\addplot[thick,blue,domain=0:4,samples=60]{30000*exp(x*ln(0.75))};
\addplot[only marks,blue,mark=*,mark size=1.6pt] coordinates {(0,30000) (1,22500) (2,16875) (3,12656.25) (4,9492.19)};
\end{axis}\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Read the purchase price and the value after $1$ year from the graph. What is the annual depreciation rate?
